From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:44:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_bcm4377: advertise wideband speech on
 the BCM4388

The driver never sets HCI_QUIRK_WIDEBAND_SPEECH_SUPPORTED, so the
management interface reports no wideband speech for these controllers
and refuses Set Wideband Speech. bluetoothd enables that setting when
the kernel reports it; without it the kernel never sends Write Default
Erroneous Data Reporting (hci_set_err_data_report_sync()), and received
SCO data carries no packet status for the packet loss concealment of
mSBC and LC3-SWB calls (BT_PKT_STATUS).

Set the quirk for the BCM4388, as other drivers do for their wideband
capable controllers. What the controller does is still decided by its
own capability bits: transparent SCO data needs the LMP transparent SCO
and eSCO features (sco.c), and erroneous data reporting needs its LMP
feature and command bits (hci_sync.c); the quirk only lets them be used.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c
index dc24c3e505..46f0f933bf 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c
@@ -534,6 +534,7 @@ struct bcm4377_hw {
 	unsigned long broken_mws_transport_config : 1;
 	unsigned long broken_le_coded : 1;
 	unsigned long broken_le_ext_adv_report_phy : 1;
+	unsigned long wideband_speech : 1;
 
 	int (*send_calibration)(struct bcm4377_data *bcm4377);
 	int (*send_ptb)(struct bcm4377_data *bcm4377,
@@ -3076,6 +3077,8 @@ static int bcm4377_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev, const struct pci_device_id *id)
 		hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_LE_CODED);
 	if (bcm4377->hw->broken_le_ext_adv_report_phy)
 		hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_FIXUP_LE_EXT_ADV_REPORT_PHY);
+	if (bcm4377->hw->wideband_speech)
+		hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_WIDEBAND_SPEECH_SUPPORTED);
 
 	hci_set_brcm_capable(hdev);
 
@@ -3274,6 +3277,7 @@ static const struct bcm4377_hw bcm4377_hw_variants[] = {
 		.broken_mws_transport_config = true,
 		.broken_le_coded = true,
 		.broken_le_ext_adv_report_phy = true,
+		.wideband_speech = true,
 		.send_calibration = bcm4388_send_calibration,
 		.send_ptb = bcm4378_send_ptb,
 	},
